Notes
- The validator is strict by design; it fails fast and returns a single, deterministic first-fail error with minimal context.
- Staleness marks the wind (and any other real-time fields) as withheld in downstream composition; you can refine which fields are considered “stale-critical.”
- Severe-weather halving of freshness is stubbed (severe=False); you can wire it to an external alert signal.
- For domains beyond weather, you can reuse the same envelope and numeric/key hygiene, swapping the schema and unit conversions.

